---
/**
 * Join the Chapter.
 *
 * Consolidates four legacy pages. The membership pitch was split across
 * "Membership" (three sentences and no next step), "VVA 227 Chapter membership"
 * (a pasted recruiting email telling the reader to complete "the attached
 * application", which was attached to nothing), "Membership Invitation" (filed
 * as a child of Fairfax Court), and the application PDF itself — which lived in
 * the sidebar of a page about restoring a memorial plaque in Maryland.
 *
 * Bill Lynch's own words are kept where they are better than anything a
 * redesign would write.
 */
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import HeroBand from '../../components/HeroBand.astro';
import MeetingCard from '../../components/MeetingCard.astro';
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';
import CardGrid from '../../components/CardGrid.astro';
import ReviewNote from '../../components/ReviewNote.astro';
import ContactList from '../../components/ContactList.astro';
import events from '../../data/events.json';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Join the Chapter"
  description="Membership in VVA Chapter 227 is open to anyone who served during the Vietnam era. Life membership is $50, once, with no further dues."
  hero
>
  <HeroBand
    slot="hero"
    eyebrow="Membership"
    title="Join the Chapter"
    lede="Life membership is $50. You pay it once and never again. In-country service is not required."
    primary={{ label: 'Come to a meeting', href: '/events' }}
    secondary={{ label: 'AVVA membership', href: '/join/avva' }}
  />

  <!-- ---------- Eligibility ---------- -->
  <section class="stack">
    <h2>Who can join</h2>
    <p>
      Membership is open to any service member who served during the Vietnam era. Where you served does not matter.
      As the chapter&rsquo;s membership director puts it:
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        It does not matter whether they served in-country or elsewhere. Someone had to keep the bullets flowing and
        the Russians out of Europe. We have two members who served on missile crews in Germany. Admiral Zumwalt,
        deceased, was a member even after he moved to North Carolina. Our ranks range from privates to a three-star
        general and admiral.
      </p>
      <cite>Bill Lynch, membership director</cite>
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      The chapter itself serves more broadly than it recruits: it helps homeless and needy veterans across Northern
      Virginia, not only Vietnam veterans.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- Cost and benefits ---------- -->
  <section class="stack">
    <h2>What it costs, and what you get</h2>
    <div class="price">
      <p class="price__amount">$50</p>
      <p class="price__label">Life membership &mdash; a single payment, no additional fees ever</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="benefits">
      <li><strong>The VVA Veteran</strong> — the national magazine, mailed to you</li>
      <li>A weekly email from VVA National with links to key veteran resources</li>
      <li><strong>The Journey</strong> — the chapter newsletter</li>
      <li>Nine dinner meetings a year with a speaker, open to spouses and guests</li>
      <li>A vote in chapter elections at the April annual meeting</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- How to join ---------- -->
  <section class="stack">
    <h2>How to join</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Fill in the application</h3>
        <p>
          <a class="doc" href="/docs/vva227-membership-application.pdf">
            Download the membership application <span>PDF</span>
          </a>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Add payment</h3>
        <p>
          Enclose a check made out to <strong>Vietnam Veterans of America</strong>, or fill in the credit card
          section on the application itself.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Include a copy of your DD214</h3>
        <p>You may black out your Social Security number.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Mail it to the membership director</h3>
        <p>He processes the application and tracks it through VVA headquarters.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <ReviewNote topic="Where applications are mailed">
      <p>
        The current site publishes a board member&rsquo;s <strong>home street address</strong> as the public mail-to
        for applications, and prints it with a malformed ZIP+4. That address is not reproduced here.
      </p>
      <p>
        The chapter should decide whether to keep using a private home address or route applications to the P.O. box
        in Arlington. Whichever it chooses, the correct address goes in this step.
      </p>
    </ReviewNote>

    <ReviewNote topic="Application form date">
      The only application on the site is titled &ldquo;revised 2018&rdquo; and its filename carries a Windows
      duplicate suffix. Please confirm it is still the current VVA form.
    </ReviewNote>

    <h3 class="contact-heading">Questions</h3>
    <ContactList only={['membership']} />
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- Meetings ---------- -->
  <section class="stack">
    <h2>Come to a meeting first</h2>
    <p>
      You are welcome at a meeting before you join anything. Come for dinner, hear the speaker, and see whether the
      room suits you.
    </p>
    <MeetingCard showReview={false} />
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- Where to find us ---------- -->
  <section class="stack">
    <h2>Where to find us</h2>
    <p>Chapter members staff tables out in the community through the year.</p>
    <CardGrid min="18rem">
      {
        events.outreach.map((item) => (
          <Card title={item.title}>
            <p>{item.description}</p>
          </Card>
        ))
      }
      <Card title="Associates of VVA" href="/join/avva" eyebrow="For family and friends">
        <p>
          Not a veteran, or a spouse who wants in? AVVA membership is open to anyone who works toward the same goals.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </CardGrid>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  section + section {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-8);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-block-end: var(--s-4);
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: var(--s-5);
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--c-gold);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--t-lg);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--c-ink-soft);
    max-width: var(--w-prose);
  }

  blockquote cite {
    display: block;
    margin-block-start: var(--s-3);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--c-ink-faint);
  }

  p {
    max-width: var(--w-prose);
  }

  /* ---- Price ---- */

  .price {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding: var(--s-5) var(--s-6);
    background: var(--c-primary-tint);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
  }

  .price__amount {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--t-3xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--c-primary-dark);
  }

  .price__label {
    font-size: var(--t-lg);
    color: var(--c-primary-dark);
  }

  .benefits {
    max-width: var(--w-prose);
    padding-inline-start: var(--s-5);
  }

  .benefits li + li {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-2);
  }

  /* ---- Steps ---- */

  .steps {
    counter-reset: step;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: var(--w-prose);
  }

  .steps > li {
    position: relative;
    counter-increment: step;
    padding-inline-start: var(--s-8);
    padding-block-end: var(--s-5);
    border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--c-border);
    margin-inline-start: 1.1rem;
  }

  .steps > li:last-child {
    border-inline-start-color: transparent;
    padding-block-end: 0;
  }

  .steps > li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline-start: -1.15rem;
    inset-block-start: 0;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    inline-size: 2.25rem;
    block-size: 2.25rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--c-primary);
    color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .steps h3 {
    font-size: var(--t-lg);
    line-height: 2.25rem;
  }

  .steps p {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-2);
  }

  .doc {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    padding: var(--s-3) var(--s-5);
    background: var(--c-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--c-ink);
  }

  .doc:hover {
    border-color: var(--c-primary);
    background: var(--c-primary-tint);
    color: var(--c-primary-dark);
  }

  .doc span {
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--c-ink-faint);
  }

  .contact-heading {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-6);
    margin-block-end: var(--s-4);
  }
</style>
